---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Related from "../components/Related.astro";
import { SITE, IDENTITY } from "../lib/site.ts";

/**
 * TERMS AND A DISCLAIMER, ON ONE PAGE, BECAUSE THERE IS ALMOST NOTHING TO SAY.
 *
 * Added after a third-party assessment listed "Terms of Service, Privacy Policy and a
 * Disclaimer stating the site provides no financial or custodial services" among the things
 * that would raise trust. Two of the three were already here. The third is worth adding for a
 * reason that has nothing to do with box-ticking: on this site the disclaimer is TRUE in a
 * structural sense rather than a legal one. A site that cannot take a deposit is not promising
 * not to; it is describing what it is.
 *
 * The same assessment recommended a legal entity and a registered address. That is refused, on
 * the page, in writing — see below. There is no company, and inventing one would be the single
 * most falsifiable claim this site could make. A stated absence is stronger than an invented
 * presence, and it is checkable: there is no registration to find.
 *
 * Deliberately short. Terms that nobody reads are not a trust signal, and length here would be
 * padding around three real sentences.
 */
const title = "Terms and disclaimer";
const description =
  `${SITE.name} provides no financial, custodial or advisory service. It holds nothing, ` +
  `receives nothing and cannot execute anything. What the site is, in plain terms.`;
---

<Base title={title} description={description} crumb={{ href: "/about", label: "About", current: "Terms and disclaimer" }}>
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="crumb"><a href="/about">About</a> › Terms and disclaimer</p>
    <h1>Terms and disclaimer</h1>
  </div>

  <p class="prose">
    This page is short because there is little to agree to. {SITE.name} publishes numbers as
    ordinary web pages. It does not hold anything of yours, cannot receive anything from you,
    and asks nothing of you.
  </p>

  <h2 class="section">No financial service, in the structural sense</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    {SITE.name} is <strong>not</strong> an exchange, broker, dealer, custodian, wallet, payment
    processor or investment adviser, and provides no financial, custodial or advisory service of
    any kind. It executes no orders, holds no funds or assets for anyone, and offers no
    mechanism by which money or credentials could reach it — there is no account, no deposit
    path, no wallet connection, no payment form and nothing to sign.
  </p>
  <p class="prose">
    That is a description of how the site is built rather than a promise about how it behaves,
    which means you do not have to believe it.
    {" "}<a class="link" href="/about">About</a> lists the ways to check each part in your own
    browser in under a minute.
  </p>

  <h2 class="section">Nothing here is advice</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    Everything published is market data and arithmetic on market data. None of it is investment,
    financial, legal or tax advice, a recommendation, a solicitation, or an opinion about what
    anyone should do. Figures described as <em>modelled</em> — liquidation levels in particular —
    are the output of stated assumptions applied to public inputs, printed alongside those
    assumptions, and are not predictions.
    {" "}<a class="link" href="/methodology">Methodology</a> shows the arithmetic.
  </p>

  <h2 class="section">Accuracy, and its limits</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    The data comes from third-party endpoints named on
    {" "}<a class="link" href="/data-sources">Data sources</a>, and is republished as received
    apart from the normalisation described in the methodology. Upstreams fail, lag and revise;
    {" "}<a class="link" href="/status">Status</a> publishes the real success rate of the ingest,
    failures included. Every figure states its own age. No warranty of accuracy, completeness or
    fitness for any purpose is offered, and decisions taken on the basis of anything here are
    yours alone.
  </p>
  <p class="prose">
    If a number here disagrees with the venue it came from, that is a bug and we want to know:
    {" "}<!--email_off--><a class="link" href={`mailto:${IDENTITY.contact}`}>{IDENTITY.contact}</a><!--email_on-->.
  </p>

  <h2 class="section">There is no company, and that is stated rather than obscured</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    {SITE.name} is an independently operated project, not a registered company, and it has no
    legal entity, no registered address and no corporate identity. It was suggested that
    publishing one would raise trust. It would not: a company that does not exist is the most
    easily falsified claim this site could make, and every other statement here is written to be
    checkable. {IDENTITY.founder ? `The project is run by ${IDENTITY.founder.name}` : "The project is independently run"},
    and the accountable contact is the address on this domain.
  </p>

  <h2 class="section">Use of the site</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    Read it, link to it, quote it with attribution. Automated access is welcome within reason —
    {" "}<a class="link" href="/robots.txt">robots.txt</a> states which crawlers are asked to
    stay away and why. Do not present the data as your own, and do not rely on it as a sole
    source for anything that matters. The site may change or stop publishing at any time; where
    a URL is withdrawn it is withdrawn honestly, with a 410 rather than a redirect.
  </p>
  <p class="prose">
    No personal data is collected that could be returned or deleted; what is and is not
    collected is set out on <a class="link" href="/privacy">Privacy</a>.
  </p>

  <Related items={[
    { href: "/about", label: "About", note: "What the site is, what it structurally is not, and how to check both." },
    { href: "/privacy", label: "Privacy", note: "What is collected, in specifics rather than assurances." },
    { href: "/methodology", label: "Methodology", note: "The arithmetic behind every published figure." },
    { href: "/data-sources", label: "Data sources", note: "Every upstream endpoint, its cadence, and what is deliberately absent." },
  ]} />
</Base>
